This pattern demonstrates the use of `.cross()` to combine two channels (reads and references) and then `.multiMap` to restructure the resulting tuples into named channels (`reads` and `refs`). The `extractKey` function is applied to the cross result to ensure proper key-based alignment. This is useful for aligning reads to references while maintaining metadata consistency.

```groovy
getSingleInput().cross(getReference('fa')) { extractKey(it) }
  .multiMap { 
      reads: it[0] // riscd, R[]
      refs:  it[1][1..3] // riscd, code, path
  }.set { input }
